00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.000 align:start position:0%
EU leaders have elected Poland's Prime  Minister Donald Tusk as the next  president of the european council and  appointed italy's foreign minister  federica mogherini as the new High  Representative at an extraordinary  meeting in Brussels attended by  ukrainian President Petro poroshenko the  leaders also discussed plans for  possible new sanctions against Russia  for escalating the conflict in eastern  Ukraine to school take over the job of  chairing the european council from the  incumbent herman van rompuy on the first  of december his mandate will run for two  and a half years but can be renewed once  mogherini set to become the new face of  EU foreign affairs after the current  European Commission's mandate expires at  the end of October turning to the  conflict in Ukraine the leaders ordered  the Commission and the diplomatic  external action service to prepare  possible new sanctions against Russia  the European Council says says that it  stands ready to take further significant  steps in the light of the evolution of  the situation on the ground and it  requests the Commission to urgently  undertake preparatory work together with  the action surface and present proposals  for consideration we then within a week  the EU's already introduced measures  such as travel bans and asset freezes on  certain individuals and steps to target  banks arms and energy  you
 

